{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-19900","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20754","text":"PULSE × box-and-box — Arithmetic Integration Review"}]},{"id":"blk-19901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20755","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-20756","text":" review (no schema break) · "},{"id":"spn-20757","marks":["bold"],"text":"Kernel:"},{"id":"spn-20758","text":" "},{"id":"spn-20759","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-20760","text":" v0.8.0 (8 rungs, 97 laws) "},{"id":"spn-20761","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope:"},{"id":"spn-20762","text":" how the PULSE loop-manifest standard (OS-010) relates to the [&] governance kernel, what already aligns, and what additive wiring is available."}]},{"id":"blk-19902","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20763","text":"TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-19903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20764","text":"PULSE and box-and-box are "},{"id":"spn-20765","marks":["bold"],"text":"orthogonal and complementary"},{"id":"spn-20766","text":". PULSE *sequences a loop over time* (phases, cadence, substrates, cross-loop signals). box-and-box renders a "},{"id":"spn-20767","marks":["bold"],"text":"single-decision verdict"},{"id":"spn-20768","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-20769","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-20770","text":" over an un-weakenable safety floor. The kernel governs *what is allowed to happen at* a PULSE phase; it is not itself a phase or a set of phases. There is "},{"id":"spn-20771","marks":["bold"],"text":"no 1:1 mapping"},{"id":"spn-20772","text":" between the 8 rungs and the 5 phase kinds — do not introduce one."}]},{"id":"blk-19904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20773","text":"The integration surface is small and entirely additive:"}]},{"id":"blk-19905","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20774","text":"1. PULSE's 7 boolean "},{"id":"spn-20775","marks":["code"],"text":"invariants"},{"id":"spn-20776","text":" are the manifest-level shadow of the kernel's alethic "},{"id":"spn-20777","marks":["bold"],"text":"Value families"},{"id":"spn-20778","text":". They can be *checked* by the kernel but the schema needs no change. 2. "},{"id":"spn-20779","marks":["code"],"text":"closure.guarantee"},{"id":"spn-20780","text":" is already an LTL fragment — it lines up with the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-20781","marks":["bold"],"text":"temporal"},{"id":"spn-20782","text":" rung (rung 4) operators. 3. PULSE V0.2's proposed linear/affine token typing is the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-20783","marks":["bold"],"text":"resource"},{"id":"spn-20784","text":" rung (rung 8, the affine ledger) viewed at the manifest layer. 4. A loop *may* declare a phase whose body is \"run the kernel verdict\" — but PULSE does not need a new phase "},{"id":"spn-20785","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-20786","text":" to express this; it is an ordinary "},{"id":"spn-20787","marks":["code"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-20788","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-20789","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-20790","text":" phase."}]},{"id":"blk-19906","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20791","text":"Rung-by-rung alignment"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-19908","spans":[{"id":"spn-20792","text":"Kernel rung"}]},{"id":"blk-19909","spans":[{"id":"spn-20793","text":"PULSE construct that already carries it"}]},{"id":"blk-19910","spans":[{"id":"spn-20794","text":"Already aligned?"}]}],"id":"blk-19907","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-19911","spans":[{"id":"spn-20795","text":"1. alethic ("},{"id":"spn-20796","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-20797","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-19912","spans":[{"id":"spn-20798","marks":["code"],"text":"invariants"},{"id":"spn-20799","text":" booleans (π/κ/β/σ families); "},{"id":"spn-20800","marks":["code"],"text":"phase.kind"},{"id":"spn-20801","text":" enumerates what *can* happen"}]},{"id":"blk-19913","spans":[{"id":"spn-20802","text":"✅ at manifest level"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19914","spans":[{"id":"spn-20803","text":"2. axiological ("},{"id":"spn-20804","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-20805","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-19915","spans":[{"id":"spn-20806","text":"— (PULSE does not rank; PRISM does)"}]},{"id":"blk-19916","spans":[{"id":"spn-20807","text":"n/a — lives in PRISM"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19917","spans":[{"id":"spn-20808","text":"3. deontic (norm/govern)"}]},{"id":"blk-19918","spans":[{"id":"spn-20809","marks":["code"],"text":"substrates.policy"},{"id":"spn-20810","text":", "},{"id":"spn-20811","marks":["code"],"text":"substrates.audit"},{"id":"spn-20812","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-20813","marks":["code"],"text":"quorum_before_commit"}]},{"id":"blk-19919","spans":[{"id":"spn-20814","text":"◻ partial — declared, not enforced by PULSE"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19920","spans":[{"id":"spn-20815","text":"4. temporal (LTL ▸ supervise)"}]},{"id":"blk-19921","spans":[{"id":"spn-20816","marks":["code"],"text":"closure.guarantee"},{"id":"spn-20817","text":" (immediate/next_tick/eventual), "},{"id":"spn-20818","marks":["code"],"text":"cadence"}]},{"id":"blk-19922","spans":[{"id":"spn-20819","text":"✅ direct LTL correspondence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19923","spans":[{"id":"spn-20820","text":"5. reflexive (entrenched ring-0)"}]},{"id":"blk-19924","spans":[{"id":"spn-20821","text":"the manifest schema itself (which fields may change)"}]},{"id":"blk-19925","spans":[{"id":"spn-20822","text":"◻ implicit"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19926","spans":[{"id":"spn-20823","text":"6. epistemic (knows ▸ believes)"}]},{"id":"blk-19927","spans":[{"id":"spn-20824","marks":["code"],"text":"OutcomeSignal"},{"id":"spn-20825","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-20826","marks":["code"],"text":"outcome_grounding"},{"id":"spn-20827","text":" invariant"}]},{"id":"blk-19928","spans":[{"id":"spn-20828","text":"◻ partial"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19929","spans":[{"id":"spn-20829","text":"7. strategic (coalition power)"}]},{"id":"blk-19930","spans":[{"id":"spn-20830","text":"multi-loop "},{"id":"spn-20831","marks":["code"],"text":"connection"},{"id":"spn-20832","text":" graph (who can ensure a signal lands)"}]},{"id":"blk-19931","spans":[{"id":"spn-20833","text":"◻ implicit"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19932","spans":[{"id":"spn-20834","text":"8. resource (affine ledger)"}]},{"id":"blk-19933","spans":[{"id":"spn-20835","text":"V0.2 linear/affine token typing (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-19934","spans":[{"id":"spn-20836","text":"◻ draft — this *is* the resource rung"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-19935","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20837","text":"Concrete alignments (grounded in the schema)"}]},{"id":"blk-19936","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20838","text":"1. The 7 invariants ↔ alethic Value families"}]},{"id":"blk-19937","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20839","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-20840","text":" lines 180–191 declare seven boolean invariants. Each is the manifest-level assertion of a box-and-box "},{"id":"spn-20841","marks":["bold"],"text":"alethic Value"},{"id":"spn-20842","text":" invariant family:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-19939","spans":[{"id":"spn-20843","text":"PULSE invariant"}]},{"id":"blk-19940","spans":[{"id":"spn-20844","text":"box-and-box Value family"}]},{"id":"blk-19941","spans":[{"id":"spn-20845","text":"Meaning"}]}],"id":"blk-19938","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-19942","spans":[{"id":"spn-20846","marks":["code"],"text":"phase_atomicity"}]},{"id":"blk-19943","spans":[{"id":"spn-20847","marks":["bold"],"text":"π"},{"id":"spn-20848","text":" (phase ordering)"}]},{"id":"blk-19944","spans":[{"id":"spn-20849","text":"a phase runs to completion or not at all"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19945","spans":[{"id":"spn-20850","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa_routing"}]},{"id":"blk-19946","spans":[{"id":"spn-20851","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ"},{"id":"spn-20852","text":" (cyclicity)"}]},{"id":"blk-19947","spans":[{"id":"spn-20853","text":"route on the κ invariant (OS-002)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19948","spans":[{"id":"spn-20854","marks":["code"],"text":"feedback_immutability"}]},{"id":"blk-19949","spans":[{"id":"spn-20855","marks":["bold"],"text":"β"},{"id":"spn-20856","text":" (no-overwrite)"}]},{"id":"blk-19950","spans":[{"id":"spn-20857","text":"recorded feedback is never mutated"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19951","spans":[{"id":"spn-20858","marks":["code"],"text":"append_only_audit"}]},{"id":"blk-19952","spans":[{"id":"spn-20859","marks":["bold"],"text":"σ"},{"id":"spn-20860","text":" (provenance)"}]},{"id":"blk-19953","spans":[{"id":"spn-20861","text":"audit is append-only"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19954","spans":[{"id":"spn-20862","marks":["code"],"text":"outcome_grounding"}]},{"id":"blk-19955","spans":[{"id":"spn-20863","marks":["bold"],"text":"σ"},{"id":"spn-20864","text":" (provenance)"}]},{"id":"blk-19956","spans":[{"id":"spn-20865","text":"every outcome traces to a cause"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19957","spans":[{"id":"spn-20866","marks":["code"],"text":"trace_id_propagation"}]},{"id":"blk-19958","spans":[{"id":"spn-20867","marks":["bold"],"text":"σ"},{"id":"spn-20868","text":" (provenance)"}]},{"id":"blk-19959","spans":[{"id":"spn-20869","text":"trace ids flow across phases"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19960","spans":[{"id":"spn-20870","marks":["code"],"text":"quorum_before_commit"}]},{"id":"blk-19961","spans":[{"id":"spn-20871","marks":["bold"],"text":"deontic obligation"},{"id":"spn-20872","text":" (rung 3)"}]},{"id":"blk-19962","spans":[{"id":"spn-20873","text":"an obligation gate, not an alethic fact"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-19963","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20874","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive wiring (no schema change):"},{"id":"spn-20875","text":" a conformance checker can lift a manifest's "},{"id":"spn-20876","marks":["code"],"text":"invariants"},{"id":"spn-20877","text":" object into a kernel "},{"id":"spn-20878","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-20879","text":" and assert the corresponding Value laws ("},{"id":"spn-20880","marks":["code"],"text":"L1–L14"},{"id":"spn-20881","text":"). The manifest stays declarative; the kernel becomes the *executable* checker. "},{"id":"spn-20882","marks":["code"],"text":"quorum_before_commit"},{"id":"spn-20883","text":" is the one invariant that is genuinely "},{"id":"spn-20884","marks":["bold"],"text":"deontic"},{"id":"spn-20885","text":" (an obligation), not alethic — worth noting in the spec so it is enforced via the norm rung, not as a fact."}]},{"id":"blk-19964","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20886","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-20887","marks":["code"],"text":"closure.guarantee"},{"id":"spn-20888","text":" ↔ temporal rung (rung 4)"}]},{"id":"blk-19965","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20889","text":"PULSE already encodes a three-valued temporal guarantee. It maps directly onto the kernel's LTL fragment in "},{"id":"spn-20890","marks":["code"],"text":"temporal.mjs"},{"id":"spn-20891","text":":"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-19967","spans":[{"id":"spn-20892","marks":["code"],"text":"closure.guarantee"}]},{"id":"blk-19968","spans":[{"id":"spn-20893","text":"LTL operator (rung 4)"}]}],"id":"blk-19966","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-19969","spans":[{"id":"spn-20894","marks":["code"],"text":"immediate"}]},{"id":"blk-19970","spans":[{"id":"spn-20895","marks":["code"],"text":"X"},{"id":"spn-20896","text":" (next) — closes within the same tick"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19971","spans":[{"id":"spn-20897","marks":["code"],"text":"next_tick"}]},{"id":"blk-19972","spans":[{"id":"spn-20898","marks":["code"],"text":"X"},{"id":"spn-20899","text":" over the loop's cadence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-19973","spans":[{"id":"spn-20900","marks":["code"],"text":"eventual"}]},{"id":"blk-19974","spans":[{"id":"spn-20901","marks":["code"],"text":"◇"},{"id":"spn-20902","text":" (eventually) — liveness, no deadline"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-19975","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20903","text":"This is the cleanest existing alignment: PULSE's cadence + closure guarantee *is* a temporal-arithmetic obligation. No change required; the spec should simply cite the rung-4 correspondence so loop authors know "},{"id":"spn-20904","marks":["code"],"text":"eventual"},{"id":"spn-20905","text":" carries only a liveness (not safety) promise."}]},{"id":"blk-19976","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20906","text":"3. V0.2 linear/affine tokens ↔ resource rung (rung 8)"}]},{"id":"blk-19977","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20907","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/V0.2-BEHAVIORAL-TYPES.md"},{"id":"spn-20908","text":" drafts linear/affine typing for cross-loop tokens. That is exactly the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-20909","marks":["bold"],"text":"resource"},{"id":"spn-20910","text":" rung — the affine ledger where a token is either *depletable* (linear: consumed once) or *reusable* (affine/\"of-course\": intact after use). "},{"id":"spn-20911","marks":["bold"],"text":"Recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-20912","text":" when V0.2 lands, name this correspondence explicitly and reuse the resource-rung vocabulary ("},{"id":"spn-20913","marks":["code"],"text":"consume"},{"id":"spn-20914","text":", "},{"id":"spn-20915","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-20916","text":" annihilation on overspend) rather than inventing a parallel one. The kernel's "},{"id":"spn-20917","marks":["code"],"text":"resource.mjs"},{"id":"spn-20918","text":" (laws "},{"id":"spn-20919","marks":["code"],"text":"C1–C8"},{"id":"spn-20920","text":", "},{"id":"spn-20921","marks":["code"],"text":"CB1–CB3"},{"id":"spn-20922","text":") is the reference semantics."}]},{"id":"blk-19978","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20923","text":"4. An optional \"verify\" gate is just an ordinary phase"}]},{"id":"blk-19979","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20924","text":"A loop that wants the kernel to gate a commit declares a normal "},{"id":"spn-20925","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-20926","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-20927","marks":["code"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-20928","text":" phase whose body calls "},{"id":"spn-20929","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.select(...)"},{"id":"spn-20930","text":". PULSE needs "},{"id":"spn-20931","marks":["bold"],"text":"no new phase kind"},{"id":"spn-20932","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-20933","marks":["bold"],"text":"no schema change"},{"id":"spn-20934","text":" — the verdict is a phase *body*, and its result is an ordinary "},{"id":"spn-20935","marks":["code"],"text":"OutcomeSignal"},{"id":"spn-20936","text":" (or a "},{"id":"spn-20937","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationResult"},{"id":"spn-20938","text":" when κ>0). Keep the 5 canonical phase kinds intact."}]},{"id":"blk-19980","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20939","text":"What this review deliberately does NOT do"}]},{"id":"blk-19981","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20940","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-20941","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-20942","text":" add an 8th invariant, a verdict phase kind, or any required field — the"}]}],"id":"blk-19982","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-19984","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20943","text":"v0.1 schema is unchanged and remains backward compatible."}]},{"id":"blk-19985","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20944","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-20945","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-20946","text":" claim a rung↔phase-kind bijection (the two are orthogonal axes)."}]}],"id":"blk-19986","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19989","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20947","text":"Enforcement of the deontic/strategic/reflexive rungs stays in the runtime that *hosts*"}]}],"id":"blk-19988","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-19990","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20948","text":"the loop (Delegatic for policy/audit), not in the manifest."}]},{"id":"blk-19991","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20949","text":"Follow-ups (out of scope here)"}]},{"id":"blk-19992","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19994","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20950","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-20951","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-conformance"},{"id":"spn-20952","text":" checker that lifts "},{"id":"spn-20953","marks":["code"],"text":"invariants"},{"id":"spn-20954","text":" → kernel "},{"id":"spn-20955","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-20956","text":" and runs "},{"id":"spn-20957","marks":["code"],"text":"L1–L14"},{"id":"spn-20958","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-19993","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19996","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20959","text":"Fold the resource-rung vocabulary into the V0.2 linear/affine token spec."}]}],"id":"blk-19995","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-19998","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20960","text":"A worked example manifest annotated with its rung correspondences."}]}],"id":"blk-19997","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-19999","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-20961","text":"Reference"}]},{"id":"blk-20000","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20002","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20962","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/"},{"id":"spn-20963","text":" — the kernel (run "},{"id":"spn-20964","marks":["code"],"text":"node test/laws.mjs"},{"id":"spn-20965","text":" → 97 laws)"}]}],"id":"blk-20001","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20004","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20966","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/CC2-capability-composition.md"},{"id":"spn-20967","text":" — operators × arithmetics"}]}],"id":"blk-20003","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20006","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20968","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-20969","text":" — the manifest schema (invariants: lines 180–191)"}]}],"id":"blk-20005","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20008","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-20970","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/V0.2-BEHAVIORAL-TYPES.md"},{"id":"spn-20971","text":" — linear/affine token draft (= resource rung)"}]}],"id":"blk-20007","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieragitxswl2rf556qmrabst4zu4j2c5vaezh4tcoo4cmuwdvsxmgqdq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}